 [9,/\b(?:arithmetic sequence|geometric sequence|series|recursive formula|sigma notation|nth term)\b/i,'Sequences and series','A sequence is an ordered list. A series is a sum of terms. Arithmetic sequences use a fixed difference. Geometric sequences use a fixed ratio.','For 3, 6, 12, … the nth term is 3 × 2^(n − 1), and the sum of the first four terms is 45.'],
 [9,/\b(?:combinations?|permutations?|counting principle|factorials?|binomial theorem|pascal['’]?s triangle)\b/i,'Counting and the binomial theorem','Use permutations if order matters and combinations if it does not, when selecting distinct items without replacement. A binomial coefficient counts selections with no order.','Choosing 2 of 5 gives 10 groups. Arranging 2 of 5 in order gives 20 arrangements.'],
 [9,/\b(?:probability|independent events?|mutually exclusive)\b/i,'Probability','For equally likely outcomes, probability is favorable outcomes divided by all outcomes. Use a complement for “at least one” when it is easier to calculate none.','With two fair independent coin flips, P(at least one head) = 1 − (1/2)² = 3/4.']
];

